BT /F2 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 742 Tm (Along the marked path) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 713 Tm (At the trail entrance, Mira photographed the route board for her own reference and) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 698 Tm (checked it against the printed map. The wooden marker pointed toward the sheltered) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 683 Tm (ridge. Neither a tempting shortcut nor a brighter patch of hillside changed their agreed) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 668 Tm (route.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 644 Tm (They paused at the harbor overlook. Papa Bear showed Mira how the same landmark could) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 629 Tm (look different from a new angle. The footbridge seemed short from the shore and long) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 614 Tm (from above. Mira drew both views, labeling where she had stood rather than declaring) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 599 Tm (that one sketch must be wrong.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 575 Tm (At camp, they placed the tent on the designated level ground and kept the path clear.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 560 Tm (The telescope stayed in its case while they checked the tripod feet. Mira put the mug on) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 545 Tm (the low table, away from the edge, and fastened the notebook with a small clip so the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 530 Tm (pages could not blow loose.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 506 Tm (A thin cloud crossed the first evening star. Mira had hoped to see everything at once.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 491 Tm (Papa Bear suggested recording the cloud as part of the view. Her first entry was simple:) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 476 Tm (a pale sky, one bright point, and a breeze from the water. The page was already useful) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 461 Tm (because it described what they could actually see.) Tj ET
