BT /F2 17 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 742 Tm (Chapter 2: Night watch) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 709 Tm (As darkness settled, Mira lowered the lantern and turned its shield toward the table. A) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 694 Tm (small circle of warm light was enough to find the mug and notebook. Beyond that circle,) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 679 Tm (the ridge and sky became easier to distinguish. Papa Bear kept the telescope pointed) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 664 Tm (away from the sun's last glow and waited for full darkness before they began.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 640 Tm (They took turns at the eyepiece. Mira described a bright point without guessing its) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 625 Tm (distance. Papa Bear asked what had changed since the previous look. She noticed the) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 610 Tm (cloud had moved, the harbor lights had become sharper, and the pale band above the ridge) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 595 Tm (had faded.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 571 Tm (A brief streak crossed the open sky while both of them were looking up. Neither had time) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 556 Tm (to draw its entire path. They recorded its direction, the approximate time, and the fact) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 541 Tm (that it lasted only a moment. The notebook left room for uncertainty instead of turning) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 526 Tm (a quick glimpse into a grand discovery.) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 502 Tm (For a while, they said nothing. The quiet was part of their shared attention. Mira) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 487 Tm (warmed her hands around the mug, then added one last line: waiting had given them a view) Tj ET
BT /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 54 472 Tm (they would have missed by hurrying.) Tj ET
